Main memory addressing :
main memory , 2^k cells , k addressing bit , size of each cell be x , if 4 cells then 2 bits are required in cells
addresses are not physically stored, decoder in cpu

byte addressable: fro every 8 bits you have one address location.
1 byte = bits
when x is fixed it called as byte addressable ,i.e a computer memory organization where every single byte (8 bits) has its own unique numeric address.

word memory and word addressable memory
number of address lines = k addressing bit value
number of data lines = word size of the memory per cell (16 32 64 etc) or byte size.

decoder
binary to decimal to hexadecimal

byte ordering: endianness(big and little) : only in multi-byte data : applies only on primitive data type(not to strings,arrays,etc).

Memory Expansion:
use MSB(from 1st bit) high order memory interleaving , for LSB (from last bit gives even chips) low order memory interleaving.
connect decoder to chip select(which is active low)

